# Site resources

Maintainer notes live in `docs/resources.md`. Never copy them into `content/`, `static/`, a Hugo page, or a commit message that restates secrets. Hugo publishes `content/` and `static/` only.

- Photos: the file in the post folder, or in `assets/images/nongrid/`, is the input and is not published. `layouts/partials/image-set.html` publishes AVIF then WebP at the slot widths (photo 480/1200, grid 480/800, gallery 480 square, click 1600). `corn compress` is an optional resize for a camera dump. The commit hook rejects a source over 2000px or 1.5MB.
- Styles: one source of truth in `assets/css/` (sitewide bundle in `layouts/partials/head.html`, homepage bundle in `layouts/index.html`, page sheets via `partial "css.html"`). All fingerprinted — no `?v=`; `player.css` is its own sheet linked right after the bundle. Scripts likewise live in `assets/js/` via `partial "js.html"`. Colors in `tokens.css`, every `@font-face` in `fonts.css`.
- Tests: `corn test` (unit + behavior, same as CI) and `corn test --visual` (screenshots, local). Run `--visual` after layout or CSS changes; `--update` only when the look change is intended.
- Cursor: `[params.cursor]` in `hugo.toml` and `static/images/cursor.gif` (32×32). `x` and `y` are the hotspot. Delete `image` to use the normal pointer.
- Banner: `[params.home]` `bannerDir` (folder under `static/`; Hugo shuffles and preloads one per render), fallback `banner`, plus `bannerAlt`. Markup is `layouts/index.html`; `home.js` only decode-reveals. Homepage title under the banner: `displayTitle` / `displayTitleLine2`, look from `titleFont`, `titleColor`, `titleFontLine2`, `titleColorLine2`, `titleHighlight` only (`home.css` holds fallbacks). `assets/css/retro.css` adds twinkling corner sparkles on the homepage banner only — not gallery, article, or writing-index thumbs (no border/wash; GeoCities vibe, not CRT). Ghost pointer via `[params.cursor]`; homepage gold star trail via `cursor-effects.html`; click hearts + idle bubbles in `site-cursor-fx.js`. Leave the GIF alone unless asked.
- Sprites: `[[params.sprites]]` in `hugo.toml` + strips in `static/images/sprites/`. Source sheets live in `assets-src/sprites/` (not published). Shortcode `sprite`. `[params.home] logoSprite` makes that strip the home nav button (`layouts/partials/header.html`). Misdreavus is front-hover only; Kagura rows are `kagura-walk` / `kagura-down` / `kagura-attack` (wind is baked into the attack frames); Sango is `sango-idle` / `sango-attack` / `sango-boomerang` (separate spinning Hiraikotsu projectile); SkiFree yeti is the subscribe footer. Footer dock (every page): `site-footer.html` fills three slots from `layouts/partials/footer/` — homepage Sango | counter | Kagura, every other page yeti | empty | Grundo; `footer-dock.css` + `footer-dock.js` lay out, mirror, and fit the slots the same way on every page, so move a piece by changing its slot, not with per-page CSS. Homepage dock: Sango left of the ticker (idle while Kagura’s wind sweep passes; click → throw boomerang at Kagura, she goes down, boomerang returns, both recover), Kagura parks right after the slash. Re-slice with `scripts/slice-*.mjs`.
- Player: `layouts/partials/player.html`, `assets/js/player.js` (modules in `assets/js/player/`), `assets/css/player.css`. One audio chrome on every page. The bar and the ↑ are mirrors: the ↑ sits in a right-gutter column at the bottom (`--player-col-x`, `--player-float` from the bottom); while you read, the bar floats in that same column at the top (`--player-float` from the top) with only play showing; once the footer dock is on screen it moves, by one CSS transition (`.site-player--parked`, `--live`), to the footer's left gutter with stop on the mirrored column and play and skip beside it, its bottom on the dock line like the ↑. The track title is hidden for now and is planned to sit above the parked bar. The ↑ is in the same place on every page; there is no per-page back-to-top. Grundo is a footer pet (right slot on inner pages), desktop-only, and kicks for the ↑ only when on screen. Phones use the same placements and footer: bar left (clamped 0.5rem from the edge), the dock's lead slot (counter on the homepage, yeti elsewhere) centered at desktop size, ↑ right. Every player glyph is `--player-glyph-fill` (0.4) of its circle (icons in `icon.html` have viewBoxes cropped to their art); change that one value to resize them all. The toggle glows with a slow pulse while playing (`.is-playing`). `--page-gutter` (`layout.css`) is the only side inset; `body` has no margin. Phone nav: Misdreavus | centered links | Pancham. Every page shares one centered `.site-shell` column, `--middle-column` (38rem, `layout.css`); no page overrides it. Nav centered in it, media centered in it (never cap a block flush left), footer dock centered, player buttons flush in the right gutter. Inner layouts (photobook, guestbook) use `baseof.html` and `define "main"`. Music keeps playing only when the layout wraps the page in `#page-root` and includes the player partial after it.
- Playlist: `static/audio/playlist.json` is the local test list (`title`, `src`). The remote fetch URL is `[params.player] playlist` in `hugo.toml` (empty → local list only). A remote folder works only as HTTP URLs plus that JSON file and CORS. Do not call a Plex or Symphony library, a drive path, or put an API token in the site.
- Socials: `[[params.socialLinks]]` in `hugo.toml` (right nav). Per-page buttons: front matter `buttons`, the `button` shortcode, or `kind = "button"` in `[params.home.footer]`.
- Backdrop: `[params.backdrop.bottom-right]`, `bottom-left`, `top-right`, and `top-left`, each with a file under `static/images/`. Corner art is homepage-only (fixed); bottom-right image is reserved for read-me `.sword-figure` (`sword_figure = true`) and is not emitted as a fixed corner. Max size is that corner's `maxwidth` and `maxheight`; a smaller file is not scaled up. `image = ""` leaves that corner empty.
